 *    the device is the first window, so a handle names one connection;
 *  - the host's CO-LOCATED CONTROLLER. The Mac app holds two relay connections
 *    from one webview — `host-<machineId>` and `controller-<userId>-<machineId>`
 *    — and the responder skips any query whose sender is its own host bridge, so
 *    that controller structurally never replies. Verified live: a union across
 *    the room returned tools from the phone and the Catalyst app only, never

